{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军守着宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找支点之间的薄弱处；电话交换所与道路交叉口都在遭受轰击。")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in thick fog and concentrated shellfire. British Fifth Army holds a broad frontage as German assault parties search for weak points between the posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("“米夏埃尔”攻势开始。急促炮击打击炮兵、联络和支点，突击部队越过薄弱处，把顽强抵抗的阵地留给后续梯队处理。新式 MP18 开始投入春季攻势。")},
{TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire.")},
{TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire."),TEXT("坚实地面有利于迅速接近，开放射界也会惩罚没有烟幕和机枪掩护的进攻。")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，康布雷反击开始。缴获坦克尚在修理场；步枪与 MG 08/15 打开通路，野炮迎击英军装甲。"),TEXT("On 30 November, the Cambrai counterattack begins. Captured tanks remain in the workshops. Rifles and MG 08/15s open the route while field guns engage British armour."),TEXT("让投弹班从被压制的枪位之间渗入。机枪持续掩护，后续步兵负责占壕；抢到前沿后不要只顾继续冲锋，及时挡住英军增援。")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("康布雷近郊的道路与铁路通向一座重要补给枢纽。坚实田地上布满履带印，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深壕横在其间；步兵与炮兵正争夺这些接近线。")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("The roads and railways around Cambrai lead to an important supply centre. Tracks mark the firm fields between the Hindenburg Line's wire and deep trenches. Infantry and batteries contest the approaches to these communications.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("英军在康布雷的推进已经形成突出部。德军集结兵力，从薄弱地段反击，突击战术与突然炮击被用来切开尚未稳固的英军防御。")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire.")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("深泥延误反击，阵雨与低空烟雾限制射程。守军也必须为转移预留时间。")},
{TEXT("雨水漫过皮尔克姆的旧弹坑。携弹队先把壕炮弹背到前沿，机枪沿尚可通行的硬地换位。"),TEXT("Rain fills the old shell holes at Pilckem. Bearers bring mortar bombs forward first. Move the machine guns along the remaining firm approaches."),TEXT("中央支点必须有部队实际驻守。以两处枪位组成交叉掩护，让军士组织轮换；英军狙击手出现时，用烟幕打断他的观察。")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆方向的进攻已经展开。伊普尔周围的排水沟被炮火打断，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑；送弹队与伤员只能挤向少数仍能通行的道路。"),TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem is under way. Shellfire has broken the drains around Ypres, and rain spreads into the fields and old shell holes. Ammunition parties and casualties converge on the few roads that remain passable.")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆方向的进攻已经展开。伊普尔周围的排水沟被炮火打断，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑；送弹队与伤员只能挤向少数仍能通行的道路。"),TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem is under way. Shellfire has broken the drains around Ypres, and rain spreads into the fields and old shell holes. Ammunition parties and casualties converge on the few roads that remain passable."),TEXT("英军在伊普尔突出部发动新攻势。炮火毁坏农田和排水渠，雨水填满弹坑；防御越来越依赖孤立支点、机枪和能够及时投入的预备队。")},
{TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge.")},
{TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge."),TEXT("坑岸和壕肩打断火线。可利用局部遮蔽接近，坡面上的孤立小队容易被压住。")},
{TEXT("地下爆破掩埋了梅西讷的旧壕道。沿弹坑组织守军，夺回补给点，恢复与残存枪位的联系。"),TEXT("Mines have buried the old trenches at Messines. Regroup defenders along the craters, retake the supply point and restore contact with the surviving posts."),TEXT("先以机枪稳住后沿，再让投弹班靠近前方观察壕。烟幕遮住被英军看穿的交通壕，避免从同一出口连续冒头。")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("凌晨的地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军沿炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也在其中；新弹坑之间，幸存枪位仍在寻找彼此。")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("The dawn mine explosions tear open Messines Ridge. Plumer's Second Army advances behind its artillery plan, with Australian and New Zealand troops among the attackers. Between the new craters, surviving gun positions try to recover contact.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("梅西讷山脊的阵地被地下爆破和随后的进攻撕开。英军正试图在高地上站稳，残存守军向东坡支点收拢，准备有限的反击。")},
{TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets.")},
{TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets."),TEXT("低云与湿泥收窄观察。后方步兵可通过满员友壕接近前沿，不必等守军让位。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前哨失去电话联络。沿白垩路反击，恢复与各枪位的联系，打通后方交通线。"),TEXT("The Arras outpost has lost telephone contact. Counterattack along the chalk road, restore contact with the gun posts and reopen the rear communications route."),TEXT("守住中央观察壕。步枪班阻止英军抢占空壕，投弹队留待近处反击；机枪组尚未归建，炮火要留给后续集结，不要浪费在零散侦察兵身上。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("阿拉斯的炮声穿过雨雪，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮住了远处枪位；洞穴、交通壕和仍在回答的电话，将守军的各个支点连在一起。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("The guns at Arras carry through sleet as British infantry move towards the German front. Chalk heights conceal the farther gun positions. Caves, communication trenches and the telephones still answering link the defending posts.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("英军阿拉斯攻势突然压向前沿。第一线遭到猛烈冲击，守军必须依靠纵深支点和局部反击，阻止最初的突破变成持续推进。")},
{TEXT("较宽田野和残存村界适合装甲展开，薄雾仍会干扰观察。"),TEXT("Broad fields and surviving village boundaries allow armour to deploy through intermittent mist."),TEXT("湿润农田与破碎阵地交错。较轻泥泞允许轮换推进，晨雾仍削弱远距离观察。")},
{TEXT("八月八日清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在亚眠以东推进，法军攻击南侧。坦克随步兵出发，炮火切断守军增援。"),TEXT("At dawn on 8 August, Australians and Canadians advance east of Amiens while the French attack farther south. Tanks move with the infantry; shellfire cuts off the defenders' reinforcements."),TEXT("本连沿主攻侧翼推进。狙击组掩护机枪跃进，军士带投弹班穿过最后的交通壕；在雾中保持预备队，别让反击切断已经取得的进展。")},
{TEXT("亚眠清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在雾中向东推进，英军位于左侧，法军在南侧作战。炮兵、坦克和航空观察员配合步兵行动；德军前沿正设法恢复联络。"),TEXT("At dawn at Amiens, Australian and Canadian troops advance east through mist, with British troops on the left and French troops to the south. Artillery, tanks and aerial observers support the infantry while German posts try to restore contact."),TEXT("亚眠攻势以突然袭击和诸兵种协同开场，英帝国与法军向德军阵地推进，百日攻势由此展开。主攻队伍仍需要步兵夺壕、巩固和抵挡局部反击。")},
{TEXT("浓雾削短观察距离，旧壕与补给湾仍能维持前后联络。"),TEXT("Fog shortens observation; old trenches and supply bays still connect front and rear."),TEXT("晨雾显著压缩射程，湿地拖慢壕外转移。近战威胁会在能看清人影之前逼近。")},
{TEXT("三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势冲破浓雾。第五集团军正在后撤，本连须接通被截断的道路，掩护失散部队归队。"),TEXT("On 21 March, Operation Michael breaks through the fog. Fifth Army withdraws. Reopen the severed road and cover the return of isolated troops."),TEXT("夺回中央交通壕，打通后撤部队的退路。提防穿过烟雾的自动武器突击组；保护观察员，以机枪掩护反击，击溃切断交通线的追兵。")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("德军“米夏埃尔”攻势在浓雾和急促炮击中展开。突击部队穿过薄弱处，英军前沿联络不断中断；后卫需要争取时间，让纵深部队重新成线。")},
{TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire."),TEXT("较坚实的地面利于快速转移。长射界使裸露机枪危险，也给镜瞄射手留下机会。")},
{TEXT("康布雷的坚实地面适合 Mark IV 展开。坦克越过铁丝后，步兵清理残存战壕，继续向后方交通线推进。"),TEXT("Firm ground at Cambrai suits the Mark IV. Once tanks cross the wire, infantry clear the remaining trenches and advance towards the rear communications line."),TEXT("本连负责缺口侧翼的步兵地段。连续夺壕后保留机枪守住出口；炮火打散远处集结，预备队留待敌军反扑。")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("康布雷攻势用集中坦克与校射准备较少的突然炮击打开兴登堡防线。邻段装甲的突破正在扩大，步兵必须控制交通壕，防止德军切断两翼。")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("连绵雨水，深泥与积水坑。壕外速度明显下降，烟幕与雨幕共同限制长射界。")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆的排水沟已被炮击切断，送弹队挤上残存木板路。壕炮先到，野炮仍陷在后方；逐个压住湿地中的枪位。"),TEXT("Shellfire has severed the Pilckem drains. Ammunition parties crowd the surviving duckboards. Trench mortars arrive ahead of the field batteries; work through the flooded gun posts in turn."),TEXT("刘易斯组已经赶到，用它压住远处枪口，投弹班等炮火压下后再接近。每占一壕就留下守军；漫长的开阔地不适合整齐齐射式的总冲锋。")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆方向的进攻已经展开。伊普尔周围的排水沟被炮火打断，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑；送弹队与伤员只能挤向少数仍能通行的道路。"),TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem is under way. Shellfire has broken the drains around Ypres, and rain spreads into the fields and old shell holes. Ammunition parties and casualties converge on the few roads that remain passable."),TEXT("第三次伊普尔战役开幕，目标是突出部东北的高地与交通线。排水系统已被炮火破坏，随后降雨让进攻通路逐渐变成积水的弹坑带。")},
{TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge."),TEXT("破碎坡面与坑岸提供分段遮蔽。短阵雨会加深泥色，但观察条件较好。")},
{TEXT("凌晨三时十分，地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。澳新部队正在邻段推进；机枪跟上坑岸，步兵打通破碎高地。"),TEXT("At 3.10 a.m., mines tear open Messines Ridge. Australian and New Zealand troops advance nearby. Bring the guns to the crater rims and open a passage across the broken heights."),TEXT("主攻已经越过前沿，接替部队必须打通观察壕与后方的通路。新配属的投弹队借烟幕清除壕口，步枪班逐段跟进；击溃阻截的守军，让补给纵队通过。")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊的德军阵地。英军第二集团军需要把突入的部队变成稳固的防线，为后续佛兰德攻势取得观察高地。")},
{TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets."),TEXT("低云压住观察距离。湿滑壕外地面拖慢推进，壕内交通保持通畅。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势已经开始。沿白垩路推进，清除高地后方的守军，为后续部队打开通路。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive has begun. Advance along the chalk road, clear the defenders behind the heights and open a route for the following troops."),TEXT("你的连队负责巩固前进通路。步枪班先占交通壕，留一队从壕肩掩护轮换；其他专门分队尚未赶到，不要把所有人一次送进开阔地。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("阿拉斯攻势开始。英军从准备已久的地道与集结地出击，为法军在埃纳河的攻势牵制德军；最初的突破之后，纵深守军正重新组织。")},
{TEXT("撤退道路穿过旧阵地，残存铁丝挡住通路。工兵先清障，Wex 分队和机枪掩护反击。"),TEXT("The withdrawal route crosses old positions, with wire still blocking the way. Pioneers clear obstacles while Wex troops and machine guns cover the counterattack."),TEXT("别把工兵当作另一支步枪班。先清理自己需要的通路，再让喷火手借烟幕靠近失守的壕角；机枪要给后卫留下退路。")},
{TEXT("斯卡尔普的旧铁丝从白垩土中露出。工兵检查未爆弹，步兵随徐进弹幕穿过缺口。"),TEXT("Old wire emerges from the Scarpe chalk. Pioneers inspect unexploded shells as infantry follow the creeping barrage through the gaps."),TEXT("工兵检查铁丝与可疑弹药，步枪留在能掩护他们的位置。为本次出击选择五支分队的编制，给徐进弹幕保留一条联络。")},
{TEXT("运河纤道仍可通行，两侧枪位保持联络。工兵维护通路，预备队准备夺回失守的中央阵地。"),TEXT("The canal towpath remains open and gun posts on either side are still in contact. Pioneers keep the route clear while reserves prepare to retake the centre."),TEXT("把枪位藏在错开的壕肩之后。工兵维持交通，喷火队留在近处反击；不要把守军全部塞进隧道上方的狭小地带。")},
{TEXT("里克瓦尔的运河明渠横在前方。工兵沿破损坡岸接近，法军喷火分遣队清理近处掩体；烟幕掩护渡越。"),TEXT("The open canal cutting at Riqueval lies ahead. Engineers approach along the broken banks; a French flame detachment clears nearby cover while smoke screens the crossing."),TEXT("用工兵打开壕前障碍，再让法军 Schilt 分遣队清理近处掩体。澳美主攻在邻段，联络官要求本连控制隧道两侧的接近线。地表旧壕与地下通道交错，逐段查明敌军位置再推进。")},
{TEXT("塞勒河车站仍在装车，列车炮组留在切口。步兵掩护车载枪炮的侧翼，守住通往河岸的道路。"),TEXT("Loading continues at the Selle station while the train guns hold the cutting. Infantry cover their flanks and hold the road to the riverbank."),TEXT("列车需要可通行的铁轨，步兵需要列车压住远处枪口。守住中央切口，派工兵清理接近通路，把迫击炮留给靠近铁轨的敌人。")},
{TEXT("塞勒河铁路切口里的列车掩护撤运。工兵清除通路上的障碍，反装甲火力攻击列车，步兵沿路堤展开。"),TEXT("The train covers evacuation from the Selle railway cutting. Pioneers clear the approaches, anti-armour fire engages the train and infantry deploy along the embankment."),TEXT("敌方装甲列车沿河谷铁路活动。工兵先检查接近线，反装甲炮盯住炮车；利用烟幕轮换夺取切口，别让所有人都暴露在铁轨旁。")},
{TEXT("南方停战的电报已到，西线仍在交火。用机枪守住桑布尔渡口，保留预备队，掩护撤退通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("News of the southern armistice has arrived while the Western Front still fires. Hold the Sambre crossings with machine guns and keep reserves to cover withdrawal routes. Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("不要把最后的交通壕变成死胡同。工兵保持出口，机枪交替掩护；居民区邻段不批准毒气与空中轰炸，靠仍能互相支援的小队守住通路。")},
{TEXT("十一月四日，新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦城墙。桑布尔渡口仍在交火。清除敌军后方守军，为后续部队打开通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("On 4 November, New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy. Fighting continues at the Sambre crossings. Clear the enemy rear guard and open a route for following troops; gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("在村落边缘保持克制的火力，工兵先行。新西兰人在邻段城墙外作战，本连要控制通路；毒气和空中轰炸均不列入本次命令。")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale.")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("肃清敌军后沿并整队突破，或击溃敌军士气。")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear and break through with a complete section, or break enemy morale.")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("夺取中央与第一道敌壕，或迫使敌军撤退")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("夺取中央与敌军纵深两道战壕，或迫使敌军撤退")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("高积水、软泥和较宽的横向战场；铁丝把干燥落脚处分割开。")},
{TEXT("冬夜的低地潮湿昏暗，浅水散在相近的交通壕之间。"),TEXT("The winter low ground is dark and damp, with shallow pools between closely spaced communication trenches.")},
{TEXT("冬夜的低地潮湿昏暗，浅水散在相近的交通壕之间。"),TEXT("The winter low ground is dark and damp, with shallow pools between closely spaced communication trenches."),TEXT("湿冷低光照与稀疏积水；交通壕近，携行装备限制明确。")},
{TEXT("硬地延伸到破损林缘，壕角与树桩截断射界。"),TEXT("Firm ground reaches the broken woodland edge; traverses and stumps interrupt the sightlines.")},
{TEXT("硬地延伸到破损林缘，壕角与树桩截断射界。"),TEXT("Firm ground reaches the broken woodland edge; traverses and stumps interrupt the sightlines."),TEXT("较干地表便于展开，但壕角与破损树线仍限制观察。")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势已经开始。沿白垩路推进，清除高地后方的守军，为后续部队打开通路。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive has begun. Advance along the chalk road, clear the defenders behind the heights and open a route for the following troops."),TEXT("Take the central communication trench, then the first enemy position. Keep a rifle section covering the approach. Securing these two posts opens the route for the following companies.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前哨失去电话联络。沿白垩路反击，恢复与各枪位的联系，打通后方交通线。"),TEXT("The Arras outpost has lost telephone contact. Counterattack along the chalk road, restore contact with the gun posts and reopen the rear communications route."),TEXT("British troops have crossed the neighbouring front. Reconnect the central trench and first opposing post. Cover the men falling back from the broken positions to the east.")},
{TEXT("勒厄化工厂仍在德军手中，残墙间的机枪封锁着接近壕。投弹班清理壕角，步枪掩护穿过最后一段空地。"),TEXT("The Roeux chemical works remain in German hands. Guns among the broken walls cover the approach trenches. Bombers clear the traverses while rifles cover the last open crossing."),TEXT("Bombers clear the near trench corners while riflemen cover open ground. Take the central and forward posts. Machine guns remain inside the works; open the approach for the next section.")},
{TEXT("勒厄化工厂的交通受到威胁。夺回外围接近壕，以破墙间的交叉火力掩护反击。"),TEXT("The route to the Roeux works is threatened. Recover the outer approach trenches, using the broken walls to support the counterattack with crossfire."),TEXT("Keep mutually supporting posts among the broken walls. Recover two outer positions to reopen communication with the chemical-works garrison.")},
{TEXT("澳军再次进攻布勒库尔，四月战斗的残骸仍留在铁丝前。用枪榴弹压制胸墙上的守军，夺取中央补给点，接通送弹道路。"),TEXT("Australian troops attack Bullecourt again, with wreckage from April still before the wire. Suppress the parapet with rifle grenades, take the central supply point and reopen the ammunition route."),TEXT("The new rifle-grenade section lobs No.23 bombs from cover. Riflemen and bombers exploit the interval. Secure the central trench and first enemy line; keep a covered route for the carriers.")},
{TEXT("澳军重返布勒库尔，枪榴弹开始落向兴登堡防线。守住中央补给点，分散布置枪位，封锁铁丝缺口。"),TEXT("Australian troops return to Bullecourt as rifle grenades strike the Hindenburg Line. Hold the central supply point and spread gun posts to cover the gaps in the wire."),TEXT("British and Australian sections approach through the wire gaps. Machine guns cover those passages rather than chasing individuals. Restore a connected line through two positions.")},
{TEXT("凌晨三时十分，地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。澳新部队正在邻段推进；机枪跟上坑岸，步兵打通破碎高地。"),TEXT("At 3.10 a.m., mines tear open Messines Ridge. Australian and New Zealand troops advance nearby. Bring the guns to the crater rims and open a passage across the broken heights."),TEXT("Advance along the crater lips with machine guns covering the ridge approaches. Connect the central trench and both deeper lines so the relief companies can consolidate the captured ground.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破掩埋了梅西讷的旧壕道。沿弹坑组织守军，夺回补给点，恢复与残存枪位的联系。"),TEXT("Mines have buried the old trenches at Messines. Regroup defenders along the craters, retake the supply point and restore contact with the surviving posts."),TEXT("Re-establish communication around the mine craters. Recover the company route and cover the withdrawing survivors. Reconnect the remaining trench mouths before the route is cut again.")},
{TEXT("山脊上的新胸墙尚未夯实，东面的反击已经逼近。机枪掩护山脊道路，预备队接应中央阵地。"),TEXT("The new ridge parapets are still loose and a counterattack approaches from the east. Machine guns cover the ridge roads while reserves support the centre."),TEXT("Expect a counterstroke when the central height changes hands. Keep a reserve instead of sending every section forward. Secure the approach, then the first deeper position.")},
{TEXT("梅西讷失守两日，反击命令送到前沿。沿坑岸向中央推进；英军预备队仍在高地后方集结。"),TEXT("Two days after Messines falls, the counterattack order reaches the front. Advance along the crater rims towards the centre. British reserves are gathering beyond the ridge."),TEXT("Counterattack through mutually supporting trenches. British troops are consolidating the central post; reserves approach through the rear communication trenches. Reconnect two positions behind smoke.")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆的排水沟已被炮击切断，送弹队挤上残存木板路。壕炮先到，野炮仍陷在后方；逐个压住湿地中的枪位。"),TEXT("Shellfire has severed the Pilckem drains. Ammunition parties crowd the surviving duckboards. Trench mortars arrive ahead of the field batteries; work through the flooded gun posts in turn."),TEXT("Place machine guns where they cover the surviving approaches. Smoke the gaps and avoid crowding the mud-bound passages. Capture the connected line one trench at a time.")},
{TEXT("雨水漫过皮尔克姆的旧弹坑。携弹队先把壕炮弹背到前沿，机枪沿尚可通行的硬地换位。"),TEXT("Rain fills the old shell holes at Pilckem. Bearers bring mortar bombs forward first. Move the machine guns along the remaining firm approaches."),TEXT("Mud slows both armies but cannot replace a gun position. Preserve the communication trench and alternate rifle and machine-gun cover. Judge counterattacks from visible movement beyond the smoke.")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("Waterlogged craters and soft mud spread across a wider front; wire divides the firmer footholds.")},
{TEXT("朗厄马尔克的农场只剩残墙，迫击炮弹正运往前沿补给点。夺取补给，用炮火逐个压制敌方枪位。"),TEXT("Only walls remain of the Langemarck farms. Mortar bombs are arriving at the forward supply point. Take the supplies and suppress the enemy gun posts in turn."),TEXT("Rifle grenades and mortars suppress the near strongpoint before riflemen occupy it. Open two linked positions. The farther concrete posts belong to the following formations.")},
{TEXT("积水隔开了朗厄马尔克的各处据点，中央送弹路仍可通行。守住补给点，掩护枪组转移和换防。"),TEXT("Floodwater separates the posts at Langemarck, but the central ammunition route remains open. Hold the supply point and cover gun crews as they move or are relieved."),TEXT("Keep the concrete posts connected. Use communication trenches for lateral support and retake the centre and first opposing post before separate breaches become a route.")},
{TEXT("梅宁路两侧只剩焦黑树桩。炮兵集中支援短距离推进，德军预备队仍在纵深等待。夺取中央后，准备迎击反扑。"),TEXT("Black stumps line the Menin Road. The batteries support a limited advance; German reserves wait farther back. Expect their counterattack when the centre falls."),TEXT("Take the centre and the next enemy trench to complete this sector’s limited objective. Expect a counterattack against the centre. Keep reserves within supporting fire.")},
{TEXT("英军正在梅宁路林缘加固新阵位。气弹已送到炮位，反击队沿掩蔽地段集结。炮火须为接近留出通路。"),TEXT("British troops strengthen their new posts along the Menin woodland edge. Gas shells reach the batteries as counterattack parties assemble under cover. Leave an approach clear for the assault."),TEXT("Enemy guns now cover the newly won ground. Do not send counterattacking sections across alone. Close behind smoke and restore company communication through two positions.")},
{TEXT("硬地延伸到破损林缘，壕角与树桩截断射界。"),TEXT("Firm ground reaches the broken woodland edge; traverses and stumps interrupt the sightlines."),TEXT("Firmer ground allows deployment, while trench corners and shattered tree lines restrict observation.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的坚实地面适合 Mark IV 展开。坦克越过铁丝后，步兵清理残存战壕，继续向后方交通线推进。"),TEXT("Firm ground at Cambrai suits the Mark IV. Once tanks cross the wire, infantry clear the remaining trenches and advance towards the rear communications line."),TEXT("Mark IV tanks join the attachment list. Riflemen follow to clear trench mouths while machine guns cover the breach’s flank. Secure the entire company line.")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，康布雷反击开始。缴获坦克尚在修理场；步枪与 MG 08/15 打开通路，野炮迎击英军装甲。"),TEXT("On 30 November, the Cambrai counterattack begins. Captured tanks remain in the workshops. Rifles and MG 08/15s open the route while field guns engage British armour."),TEXT("On the morning of the thirtieth, the counterattack order arrives. Reconnect the centre, then work through the trenches. Captured tanks remain under repair; rifles and machine guns must open the road.")},
{TEXT("布尔隆林缘的撤退纵队越来越长。夺回出口旁的交通壕，让机枪掩护最后一批部队通过。"),TEXT("The withdrawing columns lengthen beside Bourlon Wood. Recover the communication trench at the exit and cover the last troops with machine guns."),TEXT("Recover the centre and first opposing trench to cover troops leaving the woodland edge. Keep machine guns by the exit until the following men pass. Do not abandon them in the open.")},
{TEXT("英军正从布尔隆突出部撤出，德军机枪封锁了道路。接通炮兵联络，逐段接近林缘出口。"),TEXT("British troops withdraw from the Bourlon salient as German machine guns block the roads. Restore artillery contact and work towards the exit at the wood’s edge."),TEXT("Cover the woodland exit without losing support from the rear. Expect a counterstroke for the communication route. Two linked posts matter more than an unsupported pursuit.")},
{TEXT("冬夜巡逻仅配属轻装部队与烟幕。沿低地接近前哨，用烟幕掩护暴露地段；本次没有装甲、重炮或飞机支援。"),TEXT("The winter night patrol has light troops and smoke only. Approach the outpost through low ground and screen exposed stretches. No armour, heavy guns or aircraft are assigned."),TEXT("Secure the centre and enemy outpost. Tanks, field artillery and air missions are not attached to this small raid. Riflemen, bombers and smoke must carry the short action.")},
{TEXT("铁丝前出现新脚印，前哨尚未回应。轻装分队沿低地接近，用烟幕掩护通路；本次没有重炮或装甲支援。"),TEXT("Fresh tracks appear before the wire and the outpost has not answered. Light sections approach through low ground under smoke. No heavy guns or armour are assigned."),TEXT("Patrols report activity at the opposing outpost. Restore observation through the centre and near post. No tanks, field artillery or aircraft answer this raid’s orders.")},
{TEXT("冬夜的低地潮湿昏暗，浅水散在相近的交通壕之间。"),TEXT("The winter low ground is dark and damp, with shallow pools between closely spaced communication trenches."),TEXT("Cold, wet ground and low light favour a compact action with restricted attachments.")},
{TEXT("三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势冲破浓雾。第五集团军正在后撤，本连须接通被截断的道路，掩护失散部队归队。"),TEXT("On 21 March, Operation Michael breaks through the fog. Fifth Army withdraws. Reopen the severed road and cover the return of isolated troops."),TEXT("Retake the centre and next post to reconnect the withdrawal route. Machine guns cover relief behind smoke. Fifth Army is still falling back; link the men on either side of the breach.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势的炮火正向纵深延伸。突击队穿过雾中的缺口，A7V 与机枪跟进。夺取中央补给点，维持后续攻势。"),TEXT("Operation Michael’s guns reach deeper into the defence. Assault troops pass through gaps in the fog, followed by A7Vs and machine guns. Take the central supply point to sustain the advance."),TEXT("A7V tanks become available to the company. Keep infantry with the armour. Reopen the forward supply bay before pushing deeper so ammunition can follow.")},
{TEXT("利斯河低地失去电话联络，葡萄牙邻段已被突破。沿河沟恢复各据点之间的联系，夺回道路交叉口。"),TEXT("Telephone contact is lost in the Lys lowlands and the neighbouring Portuguese sector has been broken. Restore contact between posts along the ditches and retake the road junction."),TEXT("The flank connection is broken. Retake the centre and first post, smoking the road junction. The pressure on the Portuguese neighbour shows why isolated gun positions cannot hold a line.")},
{TEXT("乔治特攻势穿过河沟与低地。送弹队仍在后方涉水；机枪和突击队须互相接应，打开下一段道路。"),TEXT("Operation Georgette crosses ditches and low ground. Ammunition parties struggle through the water behind. Guns and assault troops must support each other into the next approach."),TEXT("Approach through the road gaps and watch for guns beyond smoke. Take two connected posts for the following troops. Keep carriers from falling behind the drainage cuts.")},
{TEXT("德军已攻入维莱布勒托讷，英军坦克正在村外交战。夺回通往亚眠的道路；澳军将在夜间反击。"),TEXT("German troops have entered Villers-Bretonneux. British tanks fight outside the village. Recover the road to Amiens before the Australian night counterattack."),TEXT("Counterattack through the village approaches. Give the anti-tank gun a view of enemy armour while riflemen accompany your tanks. Reconnect the centre and both deeper trenches.")},
{TEXT("维莱布勒托讷的进攻已进入村庄，英军坦克从近郊开火。步兵守住装甲两侧，夺取通往亚眠的出口。"),TEXT("The assault has entered Villers-Bretonneux. British tanks fire from the outskirts. Cover the armour's flanks and take the exit towards Amiens."),TEXT("Orders for the village approach have arrived. Riflemen cover the tanks and machine guns watch the junctions. Secure the route and prepare immediately; enemy troops outside the village will return.")},
{TEXT("八月八日清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在亚眠以东推进，法军攻击南侧。坦克随步兵出发，炮火切断守军增援。"),TEXT("At dawn on 8 August, Australians and Canadians advance east of Amiens while the French attack farther south. Tanks move with the infantry; shellfire cuts off the defenders' reinforcements."),TEXT("Whippets become available for the following movement. Shrapnel catches exposed reinforcements. Riflemen secure the trench mouths left behind the armour.")},
{TEXT("亚眠前沿接连失去联络。Captured Mark IV 与 Tankgewehr 枪组赶来增援，机枪掩护后卫。打通道路，让撤出的部队通过。"),TEXT("Posts at Amiens fall out of contact. Captured Mark IVs and Tankgewehr teams arrive while machine guns cover the rear guard. Reopen the road for withdrawing troops."),TEXT("Tankgewehr teams and repaired captured tanks join the company. Support the heavy rifle before firing and keep its carrier beside it. Recover the centre and first post to bring withdrawing troops into the communication trench.")},
{TEXT("斯卡尔普的旧铁丝从白垩土中露出。工兵检查未爆弹，步兵随徐进弹幕穿过缺口。"),TEXT("Old wire emerges from the Scarpe chalk. Pioneers inspect unexploded shells as infantry follow the creeping barrage through the gaps."),TEXT("Pioneers open the route while rifle grenades suppress near trenches. Choose the attachments before departure: observation, artillery and clearance each need a place in the company order.")},
{TEXT("撤退道路穿过旧阵地，残存铁丝挡住通路。工兵先清障，Wex 分队和机枪掩护反击。"),TEXT("The withdrawal route crosses old positions, with wire still blocking the way. Pioneers clear obstacles while Wex troops and machine guns cover the counterattack."),TEXT("Pioneers and Wex sections have arrived. Recover the centre and near post to preserve the rearguard route. Cover relief with smoke and keep companions beside the heavy equipment.")},
{TEXT("里克瓦尔的运河明渠横在前方。工兵沿破损坡岸接近，法军喷火分遣队清理近处掩体；烟幕掩护渡越。"),TEXT("The open canal cutting at Riqueval lies ahead. Engineers approach along the broken banks; a French flame detachment clears nearby cover while smoke screens the crossing."),TEXT("Pioneers open the obstacles along the cut. The attached French Schilt section clears near shelters behind smoke. Use the damaged bank approaches; crossing smoke blinds both sides, so check friendly positions before ordering fire.")},
{TEXT("运河纤道仍可通行，两侧枪位保持联络。工兵维护通路，预备队准备夺回失守的中央阵地。"),TEXT("The canal towpath remains open and gun posts on either side are still in contact. Pioneers keep the route clear while reserves prepare to retake the centre."),TEXT("Staggered guns cover both banks while pioneers maintain the towpath. If the centre falls, reserves counterattack through an intact approach. Reconnect the centre and near post to cover the next men withdrawing from the open cut.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河铁路切口里的列车掩护撤运。工兵清除通路上的障碍，反装甲火力攻击列车，步兵沿路堤展开。"),TEXT("The train covers evacuation from the Selle railway cutting. Pioneers clear the approaches, anti-armour fire engages the train and infantry deploy along the embankment."),TEXT("The enemy train works the cutting. Anti-armour fire covers the gun car while pioneers inspect the approach. Take the centre and next post to deny its observation of this sector.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河车站仍在装车，列车炮组留在切口。步兵掩护车载枪炮的侧翼，守住通往河岸的道路。"),TEXT("Loading continues at the Selle station while the train guns hold the cutting. Infantry cover their flanks and hold the road to the riverbank."),TEXT("Railway support can move only along the track. Keep infantry communication beside it while the train covers relief. Reconnect two positions to preserve the evacuation route.")},
{TEXT("瓦朗谢讷城内仍有平民。加拿大军逼近城郊，本连负责夺取外围道路；本次禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes. Canadian troops approach the outskirts as the company takes the outer roads. Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable."),TEXT("Secure the centre and first post outside town. The inhabited district is not a blanket target. Gas and aerial bombing are excluded; retain pioneers and observed ground support.")},
{TEXT("军车和平民挤在瓦朗谢讷城外道路上。后卫守住出口，用烟幕掩护换防；本次禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("Army wagons and civilians crowd the road outside Valenciennes. Hold the exits and cover reliefs with smoke. Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable."),TEXT("Control the outer route to cover departing rearguards. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised. Mutually supporting guns must recover the two local positions.")},
{TEXT("十一月四日，新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦城墙。桑布尔渡口仍在交火。清除敌军后方守军，为后续部队打开通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("On 4 November, New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy. Fighting continues at the Sambre crossings. Clear the enemy rear guard and open a route for following troops; gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("Bring the company’s hard-learned cooperation to the final approach. Pioneers lead, rifles occupy, armour and artillery engage observed targets. Open the complete route for the following troops.")},
{TEXT("南方停战的电报已到，西线仍在交火。用机枪守住桑布尔渡口，保留预备队，掩护撤退通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("News of the southern armistice has arrived while the Western Front still fires. Hold the Sambre crossings with machine guns and keep reserves to cover withdrawal routes. Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("The armistice order has not arrived. Reconnect the centre and near post, keeping machine guns at the exit. Bring back the men who can still return, then relieve the rearguard.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点，可立即用于条令训练。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point for immediate training."),TEXT("The company gains one research point for an immediate basic improvement.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。梅西讷两次行动的首轮野炮提前 22 秒就绪，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短 8 秒。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Opening artillery is ready 22 seconds sooner for both Messines operations; smoke rearming after the first mission is shortened by 8 seconds."),TEXT("Gain one research point. In both Messines operations, the first field barrage prepares 22 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes eight seconds less.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。皮尔克姆与朗厄马尔克的首轮迫击炮提前 18 秒就绪，首轮野炮延后 24 秒就绪。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Opening mortars are ready 18 seconds sooner at Pilckem and Langemarck; opening artillery becomes ready 24 seconds later."),TEXT("Gain one research point. At Pilckem and Langemarck, mortars prepare 18 seconds earlier; the first field barrage takes 24 seconds longer to prepare.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。开放毒气支援，呼吸器需另行研发。中央阵位易手后，敌军将反击。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Gas support becomes available; respirators require separate research. The enemy counterattacks when the centre changes hands."),TEXT("Gain one research point. Gas support is available; respirators require separate research. Taking the centre draws a counterattack.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。康布雷与布尔隆的首轮野炮提前 28 秒就绪，首轮迫击炮提前 5 秒就绪。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. At Cambrai and Bourlon, opening artillery is ready 28 seconds earlier and mortars 5 seconds earlier."),TEXT("Gain one research point. At Cambrai and Bourlon, the first field barrage prepares 28 seconds earlier and mortars five seconds earlier.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。本次仅配轻装部队与烟幕；装甲、野炮、迫击炮及机队不可用。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. This operation has light troops and smoke only. Armour, artillery, mortars and aircraft are unavailable."),TEXT("Gain one research point. Only light troops and smoke are attached: armour, field guns, mortars and aircraft stand down for this operation.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。米夏埃尔与利斯河行动开场士气增加 6。首轮野炮提前 20 秒就绪，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短 12 秒。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Michael and Lys operations start with 6 more morale. Opening artillery is ready 20 seconds earlier; the first smoke rearm is 12 seconds shorter."),TEXT("Gain one research point. Michael and the Lys begin with six additional morale; their first field barrage prepares 20 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。亚眠与斯卡尔普行动开场士气增加 4。首轮野炮提前 22 秒就绪，首轮迫击炮提前 12 秒就绪。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Amiens and Scarpe operations start with 4 more morale. Opening artillery is ready 22 seconds earlier; mortars, 12 seconds earlier."),TEXT("Gain one research point. Amiens and the Scarpe begin with four additional morale; the first field barrage prepares 22 seconds earlier and mortars 12 seconds earlier.")},
{TEXT("获得 2 研究点。运河与塞勒河的首轮野炮提前 12 秒就绪，首轮迫击炮提前 8 秒就绪。首轮烟幕后再整备缩短 12 秒。"),TEXT("Gain 2 research points. At the canal and Selle, opening artillery is ready 12 seconds earlier and mortars 8 seconds earlier. The first smoke rearm is 12 seconds shorter."),TEXT("Gain two research points. At the canal and Selle, the first field barrage prepares 12 seconds earlier, mortars eight seconds earlier, and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("本关有装甲列车参战。运河优先令继续生效，中央补给点可缩短下一轮整备。"),TEXT("An armoured train is present in this operation. Canal priority orders remain in effect; the central supply point speeds the next readiness cycle."),TEXT("An armoured train operates in this sector. Canal supply priority continues; central stores advance the next preparation cycle.")},
{TEXT("获得 1 研究点。最后两关禁用毒气与空中轰炸，开场士气增加 4。首轮野炮提前 12 秒就绪，首轮烟幕后再整备缩短 12 秒。"),TEXT("Gain 1 research point. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited in the last two operations. Opening morale rises by 4; artillery is ready 12 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm is 12 seconds shorter."),TEXT("Gain one research point. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited in the final two operations. Opening morale rises by four; the first field barrage prepares 12 seconds earlier and the first smoke rearm takes 12 seconds less.")},
{TEXT("城郊火力限制与老兵接替继续生效。夺取中央后，仍须击退反扑并肃清后沿。"),TEXT("Urban fire restrictions and veteran relief remain in effect. Taking the centre still requires defeating the counterattack and clearing the rear."),TEXT("The civilian-sector fire restrictions and veteran relief remain in force. A counterstroke at the centre blocks the final exit.")},
{TEXT("榴霰弹由两轮增至三轮，每轮仍为 3 发。"),TEXT("Shrapnel fire increases from two to three salvos of 3 shells."),TEXT("The fuze scale turns; the shell bursts above the line. Practised crews add a third three-shell salvo. Crowded infantry in the open are most exposed; deep trenches and earth still screen the balls.")},
{TEXT("无法读取存档，原文件已保留。"),TEXT("Unable to read the save. The original file has been kept."),TEXT("The record could not be read. The original has been preserved")},
{TEXT("在“%s”行动中配属。已完成的训练届时生效。"),TEXT("Assigned during “%s”. Completed training takes effect then."),TEXT("Assigned to the company at %s. Previous training remains in effect.")},
{TEXT("该编制尚未配属"),TEXT("This formation is not yet assigned"),TEXT("This formation has not yet been assigned. ")},
{TEXT("MP 18 于 1918 年行动配发，已完成的训练保留。"),TEXT("MP 18s are issued for 1918 operations. Completed training is retained."),TEXT("The new submachine guns await the spring offensive. Previous training is retained. ")},
{TEXT("行动简报"),TEXT("Operation briefing"),TEXT("Attachments and ground conditions")},
{TEXT("工兵清除铁丝、地雷和未爆弹。作业时需要停步，附近有敌军或受到压制时会中断。"),TEXT("Pioneers clear wire, mines and unexploded shells. They must halt to work; nearby enemies or suppression interrupt them."),TEXT("Wire cutters, probes and marking tape are not a rifleman's usual kit. Pioneers inspect suspect wires and abandoned ammunition, then cut a passage. They need time, and someone covering their work.")},
{TEXT("步枪与机枪掩护工兵接近障碍。出发前在作战室选定本次配属。"),TEXT("Rifles and machine guns cover the pioneers' approach. Choose the attached sections in operations before departure."),TEXT("Send pioneers to the obstacle while rifles and machine guns cover them. Once more formations become available than the front can accommodate, choose five sections in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("Wex 以短促喷流打击近处掩体。射程与燃料有限，喷火手需要掩护才能接近。"),TEXT("The Wex attacks close cover with short jets. Limited range and fuel make covering fire essential on the approach."),TEXT("The Wex delivers short bursts against nearby cover. Its heavy tank, hose and limited fuel leave the operator dependent on an escort across no man's land.")},
{TEXT("法军 Schilt 分遣队配属本连。储罐中的燃料供给短促喷流，用于清理近处掩体。"),TEXT("A French Schilt detachment is attached to the company. Its reservoirs feed short jets for clearing nearby cover."),TEXT("A French Schilt detachment joins selected combined operations in this campaign. In French uniform, carrying its own tanks, it clears close cover with flame. It is an attached specialist formation, not standard British infantry equipment.")},
{TEXT("烟幕与机枪掩护接近。喷流射程短，燃料耗尽后火力中断。"),TEXT("Smoke and machine guns cover the approach. Flame reach is short and fire stops when fuel is spent."),TEXT("Smoke and machine guns must cover the approach before flame can reach the position. Fuel is limited; this is a close assault weapon.")},
{TEXT("铁路炮火"),TEXT("Railway guns"),TEXT("Its battlefield ends where the rails end")},
{TEXT("装甲列车沿支线提供火炮和机枪支援，活动范围受轨道限制。步兵须守住铁路通路；敌方反装甲火力可击毁车体。"),TEXT("The armoured train provides cannon and machine-gun support along the branch line, with movement limited by the tracks. Infantry must hold the railway approaches; enemy anti-armour fire can destroy its hull."),TEXT("The armoured train serves this fictional railway branch. Its guns cover the trackside, but broken rails can strand its armour. Infantry must still fight for the cutting and the observation posts.")},
{TEXT("步兵保护列车侧翼，工兵清除通路上的障碍。烟幕可遮住敌方反坦克炮的观察。"),TEXT("Infantry protect the train’s flanks while pioneers clear the approaches. Smoke can obscure enemy anti-tank observation."),TEXT("Secure the railway strongpoint. Let pioneers clear the approach and deny enemy anti-armour guns an undisturbed firing position.")},
{TEXT("用反装甲火力攻击列车，烟幕掩护铁路旁的空地。工兵清障，步兵随后接近铁路切口。"),TEXT("Engage the train with anti-armour fire and screen the open ground beside the tracks. Pioneers clear obstacles before infantry approach the cutting."),TEXT("Keep anti-armour guns on the gun wagon and smoke across the open trackside. Pioneers and rifle sections should approach the central cutting in turns.")},
{TEXT("最后的通路"),TEXT("The last route"),TEXT("Bring back those who can still answer the roll")},
{TEXT("西线仍在交火，居民与部队共用村外通路。本次禁止毒气与空中轰炸，地面部队须清除残存障碍。"),TEXT("Fighting continues on the Western Front. Civilians and troops share the outer roads. Gas and aerial bombing are prohibited; ground troops must clear the remaining obstacles."),TEXT("News of the armistice has not reached every trench. Civilians remain in the villages and obstacles block the routes. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised here; prepare your attachments around ground support.")},
{TEXT("工兵开路，步枪与机枪交替掩护。守军仍可能在最后一道阵位反击。"),TEXT("Pioneers clear the way under alternating rifle and machine-gun cover. The defenders may still counterattack from their final position."),TEXT("Check restricted support before departure. Keep pioneers and mutually supporting sections in the line. When the fighting ends, let the men on the field finish their part.")},
{TEXT("战前简报"),TEXT("Before the action"),TEXT("Before you go")},
{TEXT("诸兵协同"),TEXT("Combined arms"),TEXT("Give every section a task")},
{TEXT("后方电话时断时续。机枪守住出口，步枪班接替空壕，突击队留作近距离反击。"),TEXT("Rear telephone contact is intermittent. Machine guns hold the exits, rifles relieve empty trenches and assault troops remain ready for close counterattacks."),TEXT("The rear telephone line comes and goes. Machine guns cover the exits, rifle sections relieve empty trenches, and bombers wait for a close counterattack. No single section can seal the whole front.")},
{TEXT("亚眠晨雾掩护部队展开。步枪占壕，刘易斯压制敌军，投弹班接近被压住的枪位。"),TEXT("The Amiens mist screens the deployment. Rifles take trenches, Lewis guns suppress the enemy and bombers close on the pinned gun posts."),TEXT("After Arras and Flanders, the company knows its trades: rifles take trenches, Lewis guns suppress loopholes, and bombers close under cover. In the morning mist at Amiens, all three must work together.")},
{TEXT("分批推进，保留预备队。炮击结束前，弹着区内的友军同样危险。"),TEXT("Advance in bounds with a reserve. Friendly troops remain at risk inside the impact area until the barrage ends."),TEXT("Advance in bounds and keep a reserve. Do not send your own men into a barrage that has not lifted.")},
{TEXT("春季突击训练"),TEXT("Spring assault training"),TEXT("Preparing the spring assault")},
{TEXT("突击队寻找强点之间的缺口，以手雷与自动火力夺取近壕。后续步兵跟进，守住打开的通路。"),TEXT("Assault parties seek gaps between strongpoints, using grenades and automatic fire in close trenches. Following infantry hold the opened route."),TEXT("Storm tactics preceded this new gun. Bombers already knew how to bypass strongpoints and close on a trench mouth. Submachine guns now add short bursts at close quarters; following infantry must still secure the route.")},
{TEXT("借雾接近，短点射压住壕口；换弹期间需要同伴掩护。"),TEXT("Close through the mist and pin the trench mouth with short bursts. Reloading requires covering fire."),TEXT("Approach through the mist and pin the trench mouth with short bursts. Save the drum for the breach immediately ahead.")},
{TEXT("可在作战室研究风暴突击队训练。完成后，投弹班可在 1918 年行动中换装 MP 18。"),TEXT("Research assault-troop training in the operations room. Once completed, bombing sections can receive MP 18s during 1918 operations."),TEXT("The company has not completed submachine-gun training. Fight with the existing bombing section, then arrange stormtrooper instruction in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("步枪班负责占壕与接替防线。胸墙提供掩护，穿越空地时容易受到机枪与炮火打击。"),TEXT("Rifle sections take trenches and relieve the line. Parapets provide cover; open crossings expose them to machine guns and shellfire."),TEXT("The rifle section arrives first. Rest the stock against the trench shoulder and identify the target before firing. Before crossing no man's land, leave your comrades a position from which they can cover you.")},
{TEXT("点击壕旁的小队肖像即可出击。前壕满员时，部队继续寻找前方阵位。"),TEXT("Click a section portrait beside the trench to advance. If the next trench is full, the section seeks a position farther forward."),TEXT("Select a section portrait beside the trench to advance. If the next trench is full, reinforcements continue looking for a position farther forward.")},
{TEXT("突击手携柄式手榴弹加入队列，擅长近距离清壕。烟幕与压制火力有助于接近，投掷仍有散布。"),TEXT("Assault men join the line with stick grenades for close trench fighting. Smoke and covering fire help them approach; throws still scatter."),TEXT("Bombers carrying stick grenades now accompany the rifles. They cannot throw unerringly across no man's land: their chance comes from smoke, crater lips and a trench mouth suppressed by comrades.")},
{TEXT("Mills 投弹班负责清理壕角与近处守军。手雷可越过低矮掩体，散布会危及附近友军。"),TEXT("Mills bombers clear traverses and close defenders. Grenades pass over low cover, but scattered throws endanger nearby allies."),TEXT("The company receives Mills bombs. A turn in the trench can conceal an enemy from rifle fire and make the grenade indispensable. Rain, fear and a running throw can all send it astray.")},
{TEXT("机枪压住守军后，投弹班更易接近。友军须避开投掷区域。"),TEXT("Bombers approach more safely under suppressive fire. Keep friendly troops clear of the throwing area."),TEXT("Suppress first, then close. Never send bombers alone into a machine gun's field of fire. At very close range, their grenades can kill comrades too.")},
{TEXT("MG 08/15 枪组抵达。机枪守住长射界，同伴掩护枪手；转移前需收枪，到位后重新架设。"),TEXT("The MG 08/15 crew arrives. Its gun covers long approaches while the escorts protect the gunner. Moving requires packing and redeployment."),TEXT("An MG 08/15 section is attached. The gunner controls the lane while his ammunition bearer guards the flank. Heavy equipment cannot chase every target; place it where the route is in view.")},
{TEXT("刘易斯枪组抵达，短点射为步枪班提供掩护。枪手停稳架设后开火，同伴留在身旁警戒。"),TEXT("The Lewis crew arrives with covering fire for the rifles. The gunner must halt and deploy before firing, with his escorts guarding the position."),TEXT("The Lewis section has caught up with the company. Short bursts give the riflemen a chance to raise their heads, while the ammunition bearer stays close. Machine guns already rule this battlefield; now you must choose where yours will speak.")},
{TEXT("机枪据壕掩护，步枪分队推进。换弹与转移时火力中断，需要相邻部队接替。"),TEXT("Machine guns cover from the trench as rifles advance. Reloading and movement interrupt fire; neighbouring troops cover the gap."),TEXT("Leave machine guns covering from the trench while rifles advance. Bursts and reloads leave real gaps. Do not leave a gun position to face a counterattack alone.")},
{TEXT("精确射手优先寻找暴露的机枪手。瞄准需要时间与清楚视线，近敌和压制会打断射击。"),TEXT("Marksmen prioritise exposed machine gunners. Aimed fire requires time and a clear view; close enemies and suppression disrupt it."),TEXT("Marksmen patiently seek exposed gunners and observation posts. A distant shape in the mud is not always a useful target. A clear line of sight makes a slow, deliberate shot worth the wait.")},
{TEXT("精确射手优先攻击敌方机枪手。完成狙击学校训练后，可换装射程更远的镜瞄 SMLE。"),TEXT("Marksmen prioritise enemy machine gunners. Sniper-school training unlocks a scoped SMLE with longer range."),TEXT("Marksmen join the company to watch the enemy's guns. The sergeant insists: identify first, fire second. Telescopic sights still require specialist training in the operations room.")},
{TEXT("掩体保护射手，烟幕会遮住双方视线。近距离威胁需要普通步兵处理。"),TEXT("Cover protects the marksman; smoke obscures both armies' view. Ordinary infantry must deal with close threats."),TEXT("Keep marksmen at sheltered observation positions. Smoke blinds both armies; do not expect them to identify a gunner through a dense screen.")},
{TEXT("军士提高附近友军命中率，帮助受压制的部队重整。晋升为军官后，指挥加成增强，行进中也能重整部队。"),TEXT("NCOs improve nearby accuracy and rally suppressed troops. Promotion strengthens the command bonus and allows officers to rally troops while moving."),TEXT("The command section restores contact between scattered gun positions. NCOs call pinned men back to their posts. Commissioned officers can give orders on the move, but nearby riflemen must still protect them.")},
{TEXT("军士重整附近部队，提高命中率并缓解压制。战地委任后指挥范围扩大，完成观察研习还可校射炮火。"),TEXT("The sergeant rallies nearby troops, improving aim and relieving suppression. A field commission extends his reach; observation training adds fire correction."),TEXT("The sergeant brings his command section forward. His orders can get suppressed men moving again. Once commissioned, an officer carries a pistol for protection and gives more attention to observation and command.")},
{TEXT("金星标记指挥者，银星标记受指挥分队。组长阵亡、受重压或离开范围后，指挥加成失效。"),TEXT("Gold marks the leader; silver marks sections under orders. The bonus ends if he dies, is heavily suppressed or leaves command range."),TEXT("Command sections improve nearby aim and relieve suppression. Protect the leader.")},
{TEXT("工兵排除爆炸物的速度提高 65%。"),TEXT("Pioneers clear explosive hazards 65% faster."),TEXT("Pioneers practise inspecting leads, marking suspect ammunition and cutting wire under covering fire. They open the route sooner, but ordinary infantry must still wait for the work to finish.")},
{TEXT("喷火射程略增；首次燃料耗尽后，可再喷射四次。"),TEXT("Flame reach increases modestly. Four more bursts become available after the first reservoir is exhausted."),TEXT("A Wex operator needs someone watching his hose and fuel supply. Prepared tanks sustain short bursts; riflemen must still silence the distant guns.")},
{TEXT("喷火射程略增；首次燃料耗尽后，可再喷射四次。"),TEXT("Flame reach increases modestly. Four more bursts become available after the first reservoir is exhausted."),TEXT("The French detachment hands over its fuel and hoses one by one. Extra reserves do not make the operator bulletproof. Cover the approach before clearing nearby shelters.")},
{TEXT("徐进弹幕各组推进间距缩短，覆盖更密集；炮弹总数不变。"),TEXT("Creeping-barrage groups advance in shorter steps for denser coverage. Shell count is unchanged."),TEXT("The gunners move their fire forward in stages, keeping enemy heads down ahead of the infantry. A revised fire plan closes the gaps between each lift, leaving less time for the defenders to recover.")},
{TEXT("己方士气低于 35 时，徐进弹幕、榴霰弹与轰炸任务整备缩短 22%。"),TEXT("Below 35 morale, creeping barrages, shrapnel salvos and bombing missions prepare 22% sooner."),TEXT("As the line falters, headquarters releases reserve ammunition. Low morale gives creeping barrages, shrapnel salvos and bombing missions priority for replenishment, shortening preparation for the next call.")},
{TEXT("装甲列车车体耐久提高 22%；铁路行动中的反坦克野炮整备缩短 18%。"),TEXT("Armoured-train hull durability increases by 22%. Anti-tank field guns prepare 18% sooner in railway operations."),TEXT("A dedicated line connects the railway gun crew to the front. The train remains bound to its rails, but clearer reports turn the rearguard's brief respite into another covering salvo.")},
{TEXT("铁路行动中，反坦克野炮整备时间缩短 18%。"),TEXT("Anti-tank field guns prepare 18% sooner in railway operations."),TEXT("Observers mark the train's gun positions and the railway cutting on the same sheet. Dedicated anti-armour liaison shortens the wait to silence this moving strongpoint.")},
{TEXT("所有步兵整备再缩短 8%，可与补给训练叠加。"),TEXT("All infantry prepare a further 8% sooner, combining with supply training."),TEXT("Veterans who know these battlefields guide the replacements. Preparations take less time because every man knows his place, even when he is afraid.")},
{TEXT("撤退道路穿过旧阵地，残存铁丝挡住通路。工兵先清障，Wex 分队和机枪掩护反击。"),TEXT("The withdrawal route crosses old positions, with wire still blocking the way. Pioneers clear obstacles while Wex troops and machine guns cover the counterattack."),TEXT("Pioneers are more than another rifle section. Clear the route you need, then let the flamethrowers approach a lost trench corner behind smoke. Keep the machineguns covering a way out.")},
{TEXT("斯卡尔普的旧铁丝从白垩土中露出。工兵检查未爆弹，步兵随徐进弹幕穿过缺口。"),TEXT("Old wire emerges from the Scarpe chalk. Pioneers inspect unexploded shells as infantry follow the creeping barrage through the gaps."),TEXT("Pioneers inspect the wire and suspicious ammunition while riflemen cover them. Select five detachments for this operation and keep a liaison channel open for the creeping barrage.")},
{TEXT("运河纤道仍可通行，两侧枪位保持联络。工兵维护通路，预备队准备夺回失守的中央阵地。"),TEXT("The canal towpath remains open and gun posts on either side are still in contact. Pioneers keep the route clear while reserves prepare to retake the centre."),TEXT("Hide gun positions behind staggered trench shoulders. Pioneers keep communications open; flamethrowers wait close by for counterattacks. Do not crowd the garrison into the narrow ground above the tunnel.")},
{TEXT("里克瓦尔的运河明渠横在前方。工兵沿破损坡岸接近，法军喷火分遣队清理近处掩体；烟幕掩护渡越。"),TEXT("The open canal cutting at Riqueval lies ahead. Engineers approach along the broken banks; a French flame detachment clears nearby cover while smoke screens the crossing."),TEXT("Pioneers open the obstacles before the French Schilt detachment clears nearby shelters. Australian and American troops lead the assault next door; this company must control the tunnel approaches. Locate the defenders among the old trenches and underground passages before advancing.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河车站仍在装车，列车炮组留在切口。步兵掩护车载枪炮的侧翼，守住通往河岸的道路。"),TEXT("Loading continues at the Selle station while the train guns hold the cutting. Infantry cover their flanks and hold the road to the riverbank."),TEXT("The train needs clear rails; the infantry need its guns to keep distant weapons quiet. Secure the central cutting, use pioneers to clear the approaches and reserve mortars for troops closing on the track.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河铁路切口里的列车掩护撤运。工兵清除通路上的障碍，反装甲火力攻击列车，步兵沿路堤展开。"),TEXT("The train covers evacuation from the Selle railway cutting. Pioneers clear the approaches, anti-armour fire engages the train and infantry deploy along the embankment."),TEXT("An enemy armoured train patrols the valley railway. Pioneers inspect the approaches while anti-armour guns watch its gun car. Use smoke to rotate troops through the cutting instead of exposing everyone beside the rails.")},
{TEXT("南方停战的电报已到，西线仍在交火。用机枪守住桑布尔渡口，保留预备队，掩护撤退通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("News of the southern armistice has arrived while the Western Front still fires. Hold the Sambre crossings with machine guns and keep reserves to cover withdrawal routes. Gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("Do not let the last communication trench become a dead end. Pioneers keep exits clear while machineguns cover in turn. Gas and bombing are forbidden near the inhabited sector; hold the routes with sections that can support one another.")},
{TEXT("十一月四日，新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦城墙。桑布尔渡口仍在交火。清除敌军后方守军，为后续部队打开通路；城郊禁用毒气与航空轰炸。"),TEXT("On 4 November, New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy. Fighting continues at the Sambre crossings. Clear the enemy rear guard and open a route for following troops; gas and aerial bombing are unavailable near the town."),TEXT("Use restrained fire along the village edge and let the pioneers lead. New Zealand troops are fighting by the neighbouring town walls; this company must control the approaches. Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised for this operation.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("The Arras offensive begins. British troops emerge from long-prepared tunnels and assembly areas to draw German strength from the coming French attack on the Aisne. Beyond the first breach, defenders in depth are reorganising.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势已经开始。沿白垩路推进，清除高地后方的守军，为后续部队打开通路。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive has begun. Advance along the chalk road, clear the defenders behind the heights and open a route for the following troops."),TEXT("Your company must secure the approach. Rifle sections occupy communication trenches, leaving one section on the parapet to cover reliefs. Specialist detachments have not yet arrived. Do not send everyone into the open at once.")},
{TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets."),TEXT("Low cloud restricts observation. Wet ground slows movement outside the trenches; communication within them remains clear.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("Underground mines tear open the German positions on Messines Ridge. British Second Army must turn penetration into a secure line, winning observation heights for the coming Flanders offensive.")},
{TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge."),TEXT("Broken slopes and crater lips provide cover in stages. Brief showers darken the mud, but observation remains comparatively good.")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆方向的进攻已经展开。伊普尔周围的排水沟被炮火打断，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑；送弹队与伤员只能挤向少数仍能通行的道路。"),TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem is under way. Shellfire has broken the drains around Ypres, and rain spreads into the fields and old shell holes. Ammunition parties and casualties converge on the few roads that remain passable."),TEXT("Third Ypres opens against the heights and communications northeast of the salient. Shellfire has destroyed the drainage system. Rain will turn the approaches into waterlogged belts of craters.")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆的排水沟已被炮击切断，送弹队挤上残存木板路。壕炮先到，野炮仍陷在后方；逐个压住湿地中的枪位。"),TEXT("Shellfire has severed the Pilckem drains. Ammunition parties crowd the surviving duckboards. Trench mortars arrive ahead of the field batteries; work through the flooded gun posts in turn."),TEXT("The Lewis section has arrived. Use it to pin distant gun positions while bombers wait for the barrage to suppress the defenders. Garrison each captured trench. A long stretch of open ground is no place for a single massed charge.")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("Persistent rain, deep mud and flooded craters. Movement outside trenches slows sharply, while smoke and rain restrict long fields of fire.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("Massed tanks and a surprise barrage with little preliminary registration breach the Hindenburg Line. Armour in the neighbouring sector widens the gap. Infantry must secure communication trenches before German counterattacks sever the flanks.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的坚实地面适合 Mark IV 展开。坦克越过铁丝后，步兵清理残存战壕，继续向后方交通线推进。"),TEXT("Firm ground at Cambrai suits the Mark IV. Once tanks cross the wire, infantry clear the remaining trenches and advance towards the rear communications line."),TEXT("Your company holds the infantry sector beside the breach. Leave machine guns covering the exits as you capture successive trenches. Artillery breaks up distant assemblies; keep reserves for the counterattack.")},
{TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire."),TEXT("Firmer ground permits quick moves. Long sightlines expose machine guns and give telescopic riflemen their chance.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("Operation Michael opens beneath dense fog and a violent barrage. Assault troops pass through weak points as British front-line communications fail. The rearguard must buy time for the troops behind it to form a new line.")},
{TEXT("浓雾削短观察距离，旧壕与补给湾仍能维持前后联络。"),TEXT("Fog shortens observation; old trenches and supply bays still connect front and rear."),TEXT("Morning fog sharply reduces effective range. Wet ground slows movement outside trenches. Close assault may arrive before a figure can be clearly identified.")},
{TEXT("亚眠清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在雾中向东推进，英军位于左侧，法军在南侧作战。炮兵、坦克和航空观察员配合步兵行动；德军前沿正设法恢复联络。"),TEXT("At dawn at Amiens, Australian and Canadian troops advance east through mist, with British troops on the left and French troops to the south. Artillery, tanks and aerial observers support the infantry while German posts try to restore contact."),TEXT("The Amiens offensive opens with surprise and combined arms. British Empire and French troops advance into the German positions, beginning the Hundred Days. The main assault still needs infantry to capture trenches, consolidate and defeat local counterattacks.")},
{TEXT("八月八日清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在亚眠以东推进，法军攻击南侧。坦克随步兵出发，炮火切断守军增援。"),TEXT("At dawn on 8 August, Australians and Canadians advance east of Amiens while the French attack farther south. Tanks move with the infantry; shellfire cuts off the defenders' reinforcements."),TEXT("Your company advances along the assault flank. Snipers cover machine guns moving forward, while NCOs lead bombers through the last communication trenches. Retain a reserve in the fog so a counterattack cannot cut off your gains.")},
{TEXT("较宽田野和残存村界适合装甲展开，薄雾仍会干扰观察。"),TEXT("Broad fields and surviving village boundaries allow armour to deploy through intermittent mist."),TEXT("Damp farmland alternates with shattered positions. Lighter mud permits movement in bounds, but morning mist still hampers distant observation.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯攻势在雨雪中展开，英军正向德军前沿推进。白垩高地遮挡远处枪位，地道、交通壕和电话线仍将守军据点连接起来。"),TEXT("The Arras offensive opens in sleet as British troops advance towards the German front. Chalk heights obscure distant guns; tunnels, communication trenches and telephone lines still connect the defending posts."),TEXT("The British Arras offensive strikes the forward line. The first positions come under heavy pressure. Defenders must rely on strongpoints in depth and local counterattacks to keep the first breach from becoming a sustained advance.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前哨失去电话联络。沿白垩路反击，恢复与各枪位的联系，打通后方交通线。"),TEXT("The Arras outpost has lost telephone contact. Counterattack along the chalk road, restore contact with the gun posts and reopen the rear communications route."),TEXT("Secure the central observation trench. Rifle sections must deny empty trenches to the British; keep bombers for a close counterattack. The machine guns have not returned to the company. Save artillery for following concentrations, not scattered scouts.")},
{TEXT("白垩坡上的短交通壕；残雪与雨水弄湿了壕肩。"),TEXT("Short communication trenches cross the chalk slope; snowmelt darkens the parapets."),TEXT("Low cloud and wet mud narrow observation. Following infantry can pass through full friendly trenches toward the front without waiting for the garrison to move.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划推进，澳大利亚和新西兰部队也在其中。新弹坑之间，残存守军正恢复联络。"),TEXT("Mines tear open the Messines ridge. Plumer’s Second Army advances to the artillery plan, including Australian and New Zealand troops. Surviving defenders try to restore contact among the new craters."),TEXT("Mines and the assault that followed have torn apart the positions on Messines Ridge. The British are trying to establish themselves on the heights. Surviving defenders gather at strongpoints on the eastern slope for a limited counterattack.")},
{TEXT("地下爆破掩埋了梅西讷的旧壕道。沿弹坑组织守军，夺回补给点，恢复与残存枪位的联系。"),TEXT("Mines have buried the old trenches at Messines. Regroup defenders along the craters, retake the supply point and restore contact with the surviving posts."),TEXT("Steady the rear line with machine guns before bombers approach the forward observation trench. Smoke can conceal communication trenches overlooked by the British. Do not keep emerging through the same exit.")},
{TEXT("陡破坑岸与残存反斜面交错，山脊后的补给湾仍可利用。"),TEXT("Torn crater lips meet surviving reverse slopes; a supply bay remains behind the ridge."),TEXT("Crater lips and parapets interrupt the line of fire. Approach through patches of cover; isolated sections on the slope are easily pinned.")},
{TEXT("皮尔克姆方向的进攻已经展开。伊普尔周围的排水沟被炮火打断，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑；送弹队与伤员只能挤向少数仍能通行的道路。"),TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem is under way. Shellfire has broken the drains around Ypres, and rain spreads into the fields and old shell holes. Ammunition parties and casualties converge on the few roads that remain passable."),TEXT("The British launch another offensive from the Ypres salient. Guns destroy farmland and drainage channels; rain fills the craters. Defence increasingly rests on isolated strongpoints, machine guns and reserves committed at the right moment.")},
{TEXT("雨水漫过皮尔克姆的旧弹坑。携弹队先把壕炮弹背到前沿，机枪沿尚可通行的硬地换位。"),TEXT("Rain fills the old shell holes at Pilckem. Bearers bring mortar bombs forward first. Move the machine guns along the remaining firm approaches."),TEXT("The central strongpoint needs a real garrison. Arrange two gun positions for mutual cover and use NCOs to organise reliefs. When British snipers appear, break their observation with smoke.")},
{TEXT("深水弹坑与软泥之间，铁丝分割了少数干燥通路。"),TEXT("Water-filled shell holes and soft mud leave a few dry approaches divided by wire."),TEXT("Deep mud delays counterattacks. Showers and low smoke reduce range. Defenders must also allow time to change position.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的道路和铁路通向重要补给枢纽。坚实田野适合坦克推进，兴登堡防线的铁丝和纵深战壕仍挡在前方。步兵与炮兵正争夺通往阵地的道路。"),TEXT("Cambrai’s roads and railways lead to an important supply centre. Firm fields suit tanks, but the Hindenburg Line’s wire and deep trenches remain ahead. Infantry and artillery contest the approaches."),TEXT("The British advance at Cambrai has formed a salient. German forces assemble against its weaker sectors. Assault tactics and a sudden barrage are intended to cut through defences that have not yet consolidated.")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，康布雷反击开始。缴获坦克尚在修理场；步枪与 MG 08/15 打开通路，野炮迎击英军装甲。"),TEXT("On 30 November, the Cambrai counterattack begins. Captured tanks remain in the workshops. Rifles and MG 08/15s open the route while field guns engage British armour."),TEXT("Let bombers infiltrate between suppressed gun positions. Machine guns cover them and following infantry occupy the trenches. Once the front is taken, stop to intercept British reinforcements before pressing on.")},
{TEXT("坚实田地、长射界与密集兴登堡线铁丝并存。"),TEXT("Firm fields and long sight lines meet dense Hindenburg-Line wire."),TEXT("Firm ground favours a rapid approach, but open fields of fire punish attacks without smoke or machine-gun cover.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾与密集炮火中展开。英军第五集团军防守宽阔正面，德军突击队寻找据点之间的薄弱处。电话交换所与道路交叉口正遭到轰击。"),TEXT("Operation Michael opens in dense fog and shellfire. The British Fifth Army holds a broad front while German assault troops seek weak points between posts. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under bombardment."),TEXT("Operation Michael begins. A violent bombardment strikes guns, communications and strongpoints. Assault troops pass through weak sectors, leaving stubborn positions to following waves. The new MP 18 begins to appear during the spring offensive.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势的炮火正向纵深延伸。突击队穿过雾中的缺口，A7V 与机枪跟进。夺取中央补给点，维持后续攻势。"),TEXT("Operation Michael’s guns reach deeper into the defence. Assault troops pass through gaps in the fog, followed by A7Vs and machine guns. Take the central supply point to sustain the advance."),TEXT("Trained stormtroopers now receive the MP 18. Approach through the morning mist and pin the trench mouth with short automatic bursts. Machine guns and rifles must follow to consolidate; do not leave the assault section isolated ahead.")},
{TEXT("浓雾削短观察距离，旧壕与补给湾仍能维持前后联络。"),TEXT("Fog shortens observation; old trenches and supply bays still connect front and rear."),TEXT("Dense fog shortens contact distances. It favours infiltration but hinders mutual support. Drum magazines are finite; allow time to prepare again.")},
{TEXT("亚眠清晨，澳大利亚与加拿大部队在雾中向东推进，英军位于左侧，法军在南侧作战。炮兵、坦克和航空观察员配合步兵行动；德军前沿正设法恢复联络。"),TEXT("At dawn at Amiens, Australian and Canadian troops advance east through mist, with British troops on the left and French troops to the south. Artillery, tanks and aerial observers support the infantry while German posts try to restore contact."),TEXT("The Allied surprise attack bears down east of Amiens. Forward posts lose contact in the mist. Local defenders must delay the attack while the rear reorganises. Holding one stretch of communication trench can change this company's fate.")},
{TEXT("亚眠前沿接连失去联络。Captured Mark IV 与 Tankgewehr 枪组赶来增援，机枪掩护后卫。打通道路，让撤出的部队通过。"),TEXT("Posts at Amiens fall out of contact. Captured Mark IVs and Tankgewehr teams arrive while machine guns cover the rear guard. Reopen the road for withdrawing troops."),TEXT("The central trench is the withdrawal route. Disperse the machine guns and keep stormtroopers ready for close counterattacks. Identify British snipers and observers; do not empty every drum at distant targets.")},
{TEXT("较宽田野和残存村界适合装甲展开，薄雾仍会干扰观察。"),TEXT("Broad fields and surviving village boundaries allow armour to deploy through intermittent mist."),TEXT("Morning mist lies over damp farmland. Preserving complete sections matters more than a blind advance. Smoke can cover a change of position.")},
{TEXT("靶场操练"),TEXT("Range practice"),TEXT("The sergeant's range")},
{TEXT("步枪命中率提高 10%；距离、掩体与压制仍影响射击。"),TEXT("Rifle hit chance increases by 10%. Range, cover and suppression still affect the shot."),TEXT("Stock into the shoulder; then the trigger. Repeated SMLE practice teaches a rifleman to spend his ammunition on a target he can identify.")},
{TEXT("快速装填"),TEXT("Rapid loading"),TEXT("The hands remember")},
{TEXT("各类武器装填时间缩短 15%。"),TEXT("Weapon reload time is reduced by 15%."),TEXT("Charger clips and pan magazines each have their own drill. Repeated loading practice shortens the dangerous silence in a firefight.")},
{TEXT("刘易斯压制射击"),TEXT("Lewis covering fire"),TEXT("The Lewis opens the way")},
{TEXT("机枪造成的压制提高 18%。"),TEXT("Machine-gun suppression increases by 18%."),TEXT("A gunner need not chase every enemy. Short bursts pin hostile gun positions and make it harder for their crews to answer.")},
{TEXT("炮兵联络线"),TEXT("Battery telephone"),TEXT("Connect the artillery telephone")},
{TEXT("野炮整备时间缩短 15%。呼叫后的落弹延迟不变。"),TEXT("Artillery preparation is 15% shorter. Delivery time after a call is unchanged."),TEXT("Runners check the trench line and the battery prepares ammunition in advance. When company headquarters calls, the guns need less time to get ready.")},
{TEXT("投弹操练"),TEXT("Bombing drill"),TEXT("A Mills bomb round the corner")},
{TEXT("手雷命中率提高 12%，落点散布不变。"),TEXT("Grenade hit chance increases by 12%; impact scatter is unchanged."),TEXT("Bombers learn to recognise exposed places in the trench. A throw can still stray, but a close explosion is more likely to catch the garrison.")},
{TEXT("前沿补给"),TEXT("Forward supply"),TEXT("Supply parties in the communication trench")},
{TEXT("所有步兵小队整备时间缩短 10%。"),TEXT("All infantry sections prepare 10% sooner."),TEXT("Ammunition, rations and replacements come forward through the communication trenches. Better work in the rear gets the next section ready sooner.")},
{TEXT("交替掩护"),TEXT("Fire and movement"),TEXT("You cover; we move")},
{TEXT("正在射击的驻壕机枪附近，推进步兵承受的枪弹压制降低 35%。"),TEXT("Advancing infantry near a firing trench machine gun take 35% less bullet suppression."),TEXT("As the Lewis opens fire from its trench, nearby infantry seize their chance. Sustained cover reduces the pressure on men crossing open ground.")},
{TEXT("火力分配"),TEXT("Fire distribution"),TEXT("Traverse the whole parapet")},
{TEXT("机枪压制更大范围的邻近敌军，射程不变。"),TEXT("Machine-gun suppression reaches more troops near the target. Firing range is unchanged."),TEXT("Gunners learn to distribute fire along the position. Men around a pinned gun also find it harder to raise their heads above the parapet.")},
{TEXT("枪组接替"),TEXT("Gunner succession"),TEXT("Keep the gun speaking")},
{TEXT("存活同伴靠近后可接替阵亡机枪手，继续使用刘易斯与剩余弹药。"),TEXT("A surviving crewman can reach the fallen gunner and take over the Lewis with its remaining ammunition."),TEXT("The ammunition bearer must know the Lewis too. If the gunner is killed, a surviving companion moves to the position and takes over the ammunition and the task.")},
{TEXT("战地委任"),TEXT("Field commission"),TEXT("A commission on paper")},
{TEXT("军士升级为军官：指挥命中加成由 25% 升至 50%，范围扩大，重整间隔由 8 秒减至 6 秒。"),TEXT("Upgrades the sergeant to an officer: command accuracy rises from a 25% to a 50% bonus, reach increases, and the rally interval falls from 8 to 6 seconds."),TEXT("The section leader receives a commission. A Webley protects him while his orders steady the men nearby. Observer training will later let him direct fire farther ahead.")},
{TEXT("前沿观察"),TEXT("Forward observation"),TEXT("Eyes ahead of the battery")},
{TEXT("指挥组与一名存活同伴停稳 2 秒、看清目标后，野炮与迫击炮首轮提前 2.5 秒，散布缩小 30%。"),TEXT("With a living escort and a clear view, a commander halted for 2 seconds brings the first artillery or mortar salvo 2.5 seconds sooner, with 30% less scatter."),TEXT("Marksmen and command leaders learn to report what they see. A clearly observed target lets field guns and mortars deliver their first salvo sooner.")},
{TEXT("烟幕后续射"),TEXT("Smoke follow-up"),TEXT("Fire beyond the smoke")},
{TEXT("向己方烟幕区域呼叫野炮时，追加一轮补射。"),TEXT("Artillery called into friendly smoke gains a final follow-up salvo."),TEXT("Friendly smoke marks the sector that needs continued suppression. The field guns add a final salvo. Gunners cannot see their own men entering the screen; infantry must still wait.")},
{TEXT("狙击学校"),TEXT("Sniper school"),TEXT("A letter from the sniper school")},
{TEXT("精确射手换装镜瞄 SMLE，射程与精准度提高。"),TEXT("Marksmen receive scoped SMLEs with greater range and accuracy."),TEXT("Marksmen complete specialist training and receive telescopic SMLE rifles. They can identify more distant gun positions and place a deliberate shot with greater confidence.")},
{TEXT("指挥目标"),TEXT("Command targets"),TEXT("Find the man giving orders")},
{TEXT("狙击手优先瞄准可见的敌军指挥者，其次为机枪手。"),TEXT("Snipers prioritise visible enemy leaders, then machine gunners."),TEXT("Snipers watch first for enemy leaders, then machine gunners. Disrupting the opposing formation often matters more than chasing the nearest skirmisher.")},
{TEXT("战地重整"),TEXT("Field rally"),TEXT("Forward on the officer's word")},
{TEXT("收到附近指挥组命令后，推进中的步兵短暂减少 30% 的枪弹压制。"),TEXT("After receiving a nearby command order, advancing infantry briefly receive 30% less suppression from gunfire."),TEXT("Fresh orders steady nearby infantry already advancing under fire. Use that brief composure to cross the next patch of open ground.")},
{TEXT("间歇补弹"),TEXT("Ammunition drill"),TEXT("Fill the magazine while it is quiet")},
{TEXT("驻壕士兵在压制较低、连续 5 秒没有目标且弹药不足半数时，主动装填。"),TEXT("Trench troops reload when suppression is low, no target has appeared for 5 seconds and less than half their ammunition remains."),TEXT("When the trench falls quiet and ammunition runs low, soldiers reload before the next exchange. Preparation should not wait until the enemy appears.")},
{TEXT("瞄准操练"),TEXT("Aimed fire"),TEXT("Stock firm in the shoulder")},
{TEXT("步枪命中率提高 10%；距离、掩体与压制仍影响射击。"),TEXT("Rifle hit chance increases by 10%. Range, cover and suppression still affect the shot."),TEXT("Gewehr 98 riflemen practise their breathing and trigger control on the range. At the parapet, each aimed shot carries a little more certainty.")},
{TEXT("装填规程"),TEXT("Loading drill"),TEXT("Load without looking")},
{TEXT("各类武器装填时间缩短 15%。"),TEXT("Weapon reload time is reduced by 15%."),TEXT("Mud and fear must not break the sequence. Every crew repeats its own weapon drill so a full reload costs less time.")},
{TEXT("受控点射"),TEXT("Controlled bursts"),TEXT("The gun follows the order")},
{TEXT("机枪造成的压制提高 18%。"),TEXT("Machine-gun suppression increases by 18%."),TEXT("MG 08/15 crews distribute bursts within assigned arcs. Disciplined fire leaves the enemy fewer chances to raise a head or move.")},
{TEXT("炮兵联络所"),TEXT("Battery liaison"),TEXT("Reconnect the rear batteries")},
{TEXT("野炮整备时间缩短 15%。呼叫后的落弹延迟不变。"),TEXT("Artillery preparation is 15% shorter. Delivery time after a call is unchanged."),TEXT("The liaison post passes front-line calls to the artillery. Better preparation shortens the wait for both the first and later field-gun missions.")},
{TEXT("壕战投弹"),TEXT("Trench bombing"),TEXT("Bombers in the trench")},
{TEXT("手雷命中率提高 12%，落点散布不变。"),TEXT("Grenade hit chance increases by 12%; impact scatter is unchanged."),TEXT("Assault troops learn to spot exposed places beside corners and crater lips. Stick grenades may still stray, but close explosions are more likely to catch the defenders.")},
{TEXT("前运补给"),TEXT("Supply columns"),TEXT("Supplies behind the leading wave")},
{TEXT("所有步兵小队整备时间缩短 10%。"),TEXT("All infantry sections prepare 10% sooner."),TEXT("Supply parties establish an orderly route through the communication trenches. Rifles, guns and assault sections all complete their preparations sooner.")},
{TEXT("前线军官"),TEXT("Forward command"),TEXT("Orders with the leading men")},
{TEXT("士官升级为军官：指挥命中加成由 25% 升至 50%，每 6 秒重整友军，行进中仍可下令。"),TEXT("Upgrades the NCO to an officer: the command accuracy bonus rises from 25% to 50%, with a rally every 6 seconds, including while moving."),TEXT("The command leader is commissioned and issued a P08, allowing him to give orders close to advancing troops. Riflemen remaining in the trench become better at pinning an approaching enemy.")},
{TEXT("隐蔽枪位"),TEXT("Protected gun posts"),TEXT("Hide the gun in the parapet")},
{TEXT("驻壕机枪手遭枪弹命中的机会与承受的压制均降低 25%。"),TEXT("Entrenched machine gunners suffer 25% less bullet hit chance and suppression."),TEXT("Deepen the emplacement and dress the breastwork. Entrenched machine gunners become harder to hit and better able to withstand suppressive fire.")},
{TEXT("留守掩护"),TEXT("Covering detachment"),TEXT("Keep one gun behind")},
{TEXT("整壕冲锋时，有枪手的机枪组留下掩护。壕内只剩机枪组后，可再次下令前进。"),TEXT("A trench-wide advance leaves manned machine-gun crews behind. When only the guns remain, a further order sends them forward."),TEXT("When a trench advances, machine-gun sections with a living gunner remain to cover the infantry. If no other infantry remain in the trench, the guns can still be ordered forward.")},
{TEXT("烟幕渗透"),TEXT("Smoke infiltration"),TEXT("Infiltrate along the smoke")},
{TEXT("突击队在己方烟幕中推进时，承受的枪弹压制减半，并靠得更近后再开火。"),TEXT("Assault troops advancing in friendly smoke receive half the suppression from gunfire and close to a shorter range before firing."),TEXT("Assault sections withstand fire better inside friendly smoke and hold their fire for closer contact. Cross the open ground before making the trench mouth hear your weapons.")},
{TEXT("炮位测地"),TEXT("Battery survey"),TEXT("The gunner's survey book")},
{TEXT("迫击炮散布缩小。指挥组与一名存活同伴停稳 2 秒、看清目标后，野炮与迫击炮首轮另提前 2.5 秒，散布再缩小 30%。"),TEXT("Mortar scatter tightens. With a living escort and a clear view, a commander halted for 2 seconds brings the first artillery or mortar salvo 2.5 seconds sooner, with a further 30% less scatter."),TEXT("Mortar crews reconcile their survey notes and firing tables. Their rounds fall in a tighter area; the explosions themselves do not become smaller.")},
{TEXT("压制突击"),TEXT("Suppression assault"),TEXT("While the defenders keep their heads down")},
{TEXT("手雷对受到重度压制的驻壕敌军命中率提高 35%。"),TEXT("Grenade accuracy against heavily suppressed trench defenders rises by 35%."),TEXT("As the barrage pins the trench, bombers close quickly. Grenades have a better chance against defenders already under heavy suppression.")},
{TEXT("风暴突击队"),TEXT("Storm troops"),TEXT("A new gun for the storm section")},
{TEXT("突击班换装 MP 18，获得近距离自动火力。可用于 1918 年的行动。"),TEXT("Bombing sections receive MP 18s for close-range automatic fire. Available in 1918 operations."),TEXT("Spring assault sections train with the MP 18. Short, drum-fed bursts strike nearby trench mouths. The firing is rapid, but following infantry remain essential.")},
{TEXT("交叉火力"),TEXT("Crossfire"),TEXT("Make the fields of fire cross")},
{TEXT("分散驻壕的机枪同时射击时，交叉火力使压制提高 40%。"),TEXT("Trench machine guns firing from separate positions gain 40% suppression through crossfire."),TEXT("Separate entrenched guns watch the same approach. Their crossfire makes enemy movement harder. Guns crowded together gain no such advantage.")},
{TEXT("壕内自动火力"),TEXT("Trench automatic fire"),TEXT("Sweep the trench mouth")},
{TEXT("MP 18 点射也会压制目标附近的守军。"),TEXT("MP 18 bursts also suppress defenders beside the target."),TEXT("MP 18 troops practise short bursts against close positions. Defenders beside the target are also pinned by the sudden fire.")},
{TEXT("备用弹鼓"),TEXT("Reserve drums"),TEXT("Keep a full drum ready")},
{TEXT("风暴突击队驻壕时，若压制较低、连续 5 秒没有目标且弹药不足半数，会主动换弹。"),TEXT("Trench assault troops reload when suppression is low, no target has appeared for 5 seconds and less than half their ammunition remains."),TEXT("When the trench becomes quiet and the drum is partly spent, stormtroopers change it before the next fight. Close combat should not begin with an empty gun.")},
{TEXT("无法读取存档，原文件已保留。"),TEXT("Unable to read the save. The original file has been kept."),TEXT("The record could not be read. The original file has been preserved")},
{TEXT("无法备份旧存档，原文件已保留。"),TEXT("Unable to back up the old save. The original file has been kept."),TEXT("The old record could not be backed up. The original has been preserved")},
{TEXT("战役存档已更新。"),TEXT("Campaign save updated."),TEXT("Previous campaign research has been saved separately")},
{TEXT("凌晨三时十分，地下爆破撕开梅西讷山脊。澳新部队正在邻段推进；机枪跟上坑岸，步兵打通破碎高地。"),TEXT("At 3.10 a.m., mines tear open Messines Ridge. Australian and New Zealand troops advance nearby. Bring the guns to the crater rims and open a passage across the broken heights."),TEXT("The main attack has passed the front line. Relieving troops must reopen the route between the observation trench and the rear. Bombers clear the trench mouths under smoke; rifle sections follow bay by bay. Break the blocking force and bring the supply column through.")},
{TEXT("三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势冲破浓雾。第五集团军正在后撤，本连须接通被截断的道路，掩护失散部队归队。"),TEXT("On 21 March, Operation Michael breaks through the fog. Fifth Army withdraws. Reopen the severed road and cover the return of isolated troops."),TEXT("Retake the central communication trench and reopen the withdrawal route. Watch for assault groups advancing through the smoke. Protect the observers, cover the counterstroke with machine guns, and break the pursuit blocking the road.")},
{TEXT("为投弹班、工兵与喷火分遣队配发呼吸器。完成佩戴后，毒气累积减少 78%；仍受压制，久留仍可能致命。其余分队需避开毒区。"),TEXT("Issues respirators to bombers, pioneers and flame detachments. Once sealed, gas exposure falls by 78%. Suppression persists and prolonged exposure can still kill. Other sections must avoid the cloud."),TEXT("Respirator instruction begins with an airtight seal and a filter kept clear of muddy water. Once trained and equipped, the men can don their masks at the alarm and reduce losses to gas.")},
{TEXT("为投弹班、工兵与喷火分遣队配发呼吸器。完成佩戴后，毒气累积减少 78%；仍受压制，久留仍可能致命。其余分队需避开毒区。"),TEXT("Issues respirators to bombers, pioneers and flame detachments. Once sealed, gas exposure falls by 78%. Suppression persists and prolonged exposure can still kill. Other sections must avoid the cloud."),TEXT("The small-box respirator demands practice. Fit the mouthpiece and nose clip correctly; inspect the hose and filter box, and replace wet filter material. Arrange this equipment and training before the alarm sounds.")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("Capture the centre and both enemy trench lines, or force the enemy to retreat.")},
{TEXT("清除敌军后方守军，整队越过交通线；或击溃敌军士气。"),TEXT("Clear the enemy rear guard and cross the communications line with a whole surviving section, or break enemy morale."),TEXT("Capture the centre and first enemy trench, or force a retreat")},
{TEXT("反坦克步枪散布缩小 15%，命中后的击穿机会提高。"),TEXT("Anti-tank rifle scatter is reduced by 15%, with better penetration after a hit."),TEXT("The Tankgewehr demands its own support and aiming drill. The gunner steadies the heavy rifle while his carrier watches the flank. Better aim finds vulnerable armour; a hit still does not guarantee penetration.")},
{TEXT("枪榴弹落点散布半径缩小 15%。"),TEXT("Rifle-grenade scatter radius is reduced by 15%."),TEXT("The No. 23 carries a grenade beyond a hand throw. Drill with launching cartridges, the retaining bracket and safe elevation gathers the shots around an observed post. Rifle cover remains essential.")},
{TEXT("专门射手附近有存活的同队携弹手时，装填时间缩短 15%。"),TEXT("Specialist weapons reload 15% faster while a living squadmate remains nearby."),TEXT("The heavy cartridges pass to the gunner one at a time. A living carrier beside his section eases each reload. Without that companion, the gunner must manage the whole task alone.")},
{TEXT("专门射手附近有存活的同队携弹手时，装填时间缩短 15%。"),TEXT("Specialist weapons reload 15% faster while a living squadmate remains nearby."),TEXT("Grenades and launching cartridges travel separately. Between shots the carrier brings the next round to the gunner. Reloading is smoother with his companion nearby; a lone gunner loses that help.")},
{TEXT("驻守中央之后的第一道敌壕时，间接火力首轮提前 2 秒抵达。"),TEXT("Garrisoning the first enemy trench beyond the centre brings the first indirect-fire salvo 2 seconds sooner."),TEXT("Lay the telephone wire into captured ground. A section holding the first enemy trench beyond the centre shortens the first indirect-fire request. An empty post cannot maintain that connection.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯前哨的电话中断。联络兵沿交通壕寻找失联分队，连部重新标出可用枪位。"),TEXT("The Arras outpost telephones are down. Runners search the communication trenches while headquarters marks the surviving gun posts."),TEXT("The Arras outpost telephone gives no answer. Headquarters marks the guns and reserve junctions again, while runners search the communication trenches for the missing sections.")},
{TEXT("阿拉斯地道里的部队等待出发。炮兵测地表已送到连部，军士核对各班的行军路线。"),TEXT("Troops wait in the Arras tunnels. The battery survey reaches headquarters as sergeants check each section’s route."),TEXT("Troops wait to move in the Arras tunnels. The battery survey reaches company headquarters and NCOs check each section's route.")},
{TEXT("爆破震断山脊电话，反斜面接线箱仍可通话。观察员把幸存枪位报回炮兵。"),TEXT("The mines sever the ridge telephones. A reverse-slope junction still works, allowing observers to report the surviving posts."),TEXT("Explosions cut the ridge telephone, but a junction box on the reverse slope still works. Runners find an observer and report the surviving posts to the guns.")},
{TEXT("梅西讷攻击前，测绘员复核爆破点。澳新邻段送来接合部草图，炮兵据此修订火力表。"),TEXT("Before Messines, surveyors check the mine positions. A sketch from the neighbouring ANZAC sector helps the batteries revise their fire plan."),TEXT("Before the Messines attack, surveyors check the mine positions against the fire plan. A sketch arrives from the neighbouring Anzac sector, helping observers mark the opening targets.")},
{TEXT("炮车陷在皮尔克姆泥地，携弹队改用肩背运送壕炮弹。少数木板路承担了整段前沿的补给。"),TEXT("Gun wagons sink into the Pilckem mud. Bearers shoulder mortar bombs along the few duckboards still carrying the front’s supplies."),TEXT("Gun wagons sink into the Pilckem mud. Bearers divide the mortar bombs between them and carry them towards the accessible forward posts.")},
{TEXT("佛兰德排水沟被炮火切断。重炮弹滞留后方，携弹队沿木板路把壕炮弹送到前沿。"),TEXT("Shellfire severs the Flanders drains. Heavy shells remain in the rear while carrying parties bring mortar bombs along the duckboards."),TEXT("Shellfire has broken the Flanders drains. Heavy shells are unloaded behind the line while bearers take mortar bombs along the duckboards.")},
{TEXT("反击队在路口与炮兵观察员会合。气弹送到炮位，突击路线重新标在同一张图上。"),TEXT("Counterattack parties meet the artillery observer at the junction. Gas shells reach the batteries; the assault routes are marked on a shared map."),TEXT("The counterattack party meets the artillery observer at a junction. Fresh gas shells wait beside the guns as both parties mark their approach on the same map.")},
{TEXT("梅宁路的火力表划定了短距离推进目标。步兵夺取林缘后就地固守，预备队等待德军反击。"),TEXT("The Menin fire plan sets a limited advance. Infantry are to hold the woodland edge, with reserves ready for the German counterattack."),TEXT("The limited objective at Menin Road is marked on the fire plan. Infantry are to hold the woodland edge once taken, with reserves waiting for the German counterattack.")},
{TEXT("十一月三十日，德军反击康布雷突出部。野炮迎击英军坦克，缴获车辆仍在修理场。"),TEXT("On 30 November, German troops counterattack the Cambrai salient. Field guns engage British tanks while captured vehicles remain in the workshops."),TEXT("On 30 November, German troops counterattack the Cambrai salient. Field guns watch the tank approaches while machine guns cover the infantry; captured vehicles remain in the workshops.")},
{TEXT("康布雷的硬地承住坦克履带。炮兵按测算数据突然开火，步兵随装甲越过铁丝。"),TEXT("Firm ground at Cambrai carries the tanks. The guns open from calculated data as infantry follow armour through the wire."),TEXT("Firm ground at Cambrai carries the tracks. The guns fire from calculated data, infantry follow the tanks and carrying parties come up the same routes.")},
{TEXT("前沿等待对面换防的消息。轻装巡逻沿低地接近前哨，随队只配烟幕支援。"),TEXT("The front awaits word of an enemy relief. A light patrol approaches the outpost through low ground with smoke as its only support."),TEXT("The front needs word of the enemy relief. A light patrol takes smoke shells along the low approach to the outpost; heavy batteries are not taking orders tonight.")},
{TEXT("冬夜巡逻名单送到连部。轻装分队沿低地出发，炮兵联络与装甲配属已从命令中划去。"),TEXT("The winter patrol roll reaches headquarters. Light sections set out through the low ground; heavy batteries and armour have been struck from the orders."),TEXT("A few light sections appear on the winter patrol roll. Battery liaison has been struck out; the men take smoke and move to investigate the opposing outpost.")},
{TEXT("东线部队陆续运抵西线。突击训练与弹药分配令送到各连，携弹队开始向前集中。"),TEXT("Troops from the Eastern Front arrive in the west. Assault instructions and ammunition allocations reach the companies as bearers gather forward."),TEXT("Troops from the Eastern Front arrive in the west. Assault instructions, ammunition allocations and departure times reach company headquarters as the carrying parties gather forward.")},
{TEXT("米夏埃尔攻势迫使第五集团军后撤。法军靠近受威胁的接合部，补充兵带着新联络表抵达。"),TEXT("Operation Michael forces Fifth Army back. French troops approach the threatened junction as replacement drafts arrive with new contact lists."),TEXT("Operation Michael forces the British Fifth Army back. French troops approach the threatened junction between the armies, and replacements reach the company with a revised contact list.")},
{TEXT("八月八日，邻段枪位接连失联。缴获坦克与反坦克步枪接到急令，掩护后卫撤离通路。"),TEXT("On 8 August, neighbouring posts fall silent. Captured tanks and tank rifles receive urgent orders to cover the rearguard routes."),TEXT("On 8 August, neighbouring posts fall out of contact. Repaired captured tanks, tank rifles and batteries receive emergency orders to cover the rearguard's route.")},
{TEXT("亚眠火力表列明相邻部队的出发时刻。澳大利亚、加拿大、英国与法国部队在各自地段推进。"),TEXT("The Amiens fire plan fixes each formation’s departure. Australian, Canadian, British and French troops advance in their assigned sectors."),TEXT("The Amiens fire plan lists the departure times of neighbouring formations. Australian, Canadian, British and French troops advance in their sectors with tanks and aircraft supporting the infantry.")},
{TEXT("运河坡岸被炮火击破，残存纤道仍可通行。烟弹与炮兵联络优先送到后卫路口。"),TEXT("Shellfire breaks the canal banks, but the surviving towpath remains open. Smoke and battery liaison are given priority at the rearguard junctions."),TEXT("Shellfire has broken the canal banks, but traffic still passes along the remaining towpath. Smoke ammunition and battery contacts are sent first to these junctions for the rear guard.")},
{TEXT("北面的贝利库尔仍在交战。本连位于里克瓦尔明渠旁，工兵检查纤道，观察员沿岸寻找观察位置。"),TEXT("Fighting continues at Bellicourt to the north. The company is beside the open canal at Riqueval, where pioneers inspect the towpath and observers seek positions along the bank."),TEXT("Fighting continues around Bellicourt to the north as the company waits beside the open canal at Riqueval. Engineers inspect the towpath and observers look for a view along the bank.")},
{TEXT("塞勒河车站仍有物资待装。列车炮组留守切口，步兵沿路堤保护两翼。"),TEXT("Supplies await loading at the Selle station. The train guns hold the cutting while infantry guard both flanks along the embankment."),TEXT("Supplies still wait to be loaded at the station. The railway gun crew remains in the Selle valley while infantry hold the near approaches and observers watch the bank.")},
{TEXT("追击抵达塞勒河。列车火力封住切口，本连受命打通河谷，为后续部队开路。"),TEXT("The pursuit reaches the Selle. Train guns bar the cutting; the company must open the valley route for the following troops."),TEXT("The pursuit reaches the Selle, where railway guns hold a cutting. The company must clear a route through the valley for the following troops.")},
{TEXT("军车与平民手推车挤在城外道路上。老兵带领补充兵守住路口，炮兵收紧射击区域。"),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the outer road. Veterans post replacements at the junctions as batteries narrow their fire zones."),TEXT("Army wagons and civilian handcarts crowd the road outside town. The rear guard narrows its fire zones and posts veterans beside replacements at the junctions.")},
{TEXT("瓦朗谢讷仍有居民，加拿大军正逼近城郊。炮兵标出禁射区，老兵领着补充兵沿浅沟前进。"),TEXT("Civilians remain in Valenciennes as Canadians approach the outskirts. Batteries mark restricted zones while veterans lead replacements along shallow ditches."),TEXT("Valenciennes still has inhabitants as Canadian troops approach its outskirts. The guns mark restricted fire zones and veterans lead replacements along the shallow ditches.")},
{TEXT("南方停战的电报送到连部，西线仍在开火。军士沿桑布尔渡口清点等待撤离的分队。"),TEXT("News of the southern armistice reaches headquarters. The Western Front still fires as NCOs count the sections waiting at the Sambre crossing."),TEXT("News of the southern armistice arrives while the Western Front still fires. The officer pockets the telegram and the NCO counts the sections waiting beside the crossing.")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦，桑布尔渡口仍传来枪声。携弹队沿城外道路，把弹药送到下一处枪位。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy while guns still fire at the Sambre crossings. Ammunition parties carry supplies along the outer road to the next gun post."),TEXT("New Zealand troops advance towards Le Quesnoy while firing continues at the Sambre crossings. Headquarters copies the relief list as bearers move along the road outside town.")},
{TEXT("新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦，桑布尔渡口仍传来枪声。携弹队沿城外道路，把弹药送到下一处枪位。"),TEXT("New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy while guns still fire at the Sambre crossings. Ammunition parties carry supplies along the outer road to the next gun post."),TEXT("新西兰部队逼近勒凯努瓦，桑布尔渡口仍传来枪声。携弹队沿城外道路送往下一处枪位。")},
